Using the built mod in a modpack or on a server is permitted.


2. GRANT TO UPSTREAM DEVELOPERS

Most of this project exists as mixins into other people's mods. It patches, extends
and works around code they wrote and still maintain, and the best outcome for any
tweak here is that it stops needing to exist because the fix landed upstream. When
that happens, this licence should not be the thing standing in the way.

Accordingly, the copyright holders, maintainers and contributors of any mod that this
project targets with a mixin, access widener, coremod or Mixin plugin -- at the time
of writing Refined Storage, Cable Tiers, Step Crafter, Functional Storage and
Sophisticated Core, together with any mod similarly targeted by a later version of
this project -- are each granted a perpetual, irrevocable, worldwide, royalty-free,
non-exclusive licence to:

  a. use, copy, modify and adapt any part of this source code, in whole or in part;
  b. incorporate it into that mod, or into any other project they maintain; and
  c. release the result under whatever licence that project uses, including a licence
     more permissive than this one, and including a licence under which they are the
     stated author.

NO ATTRIBUTION IS REQUIRED. No credit, notice, changelog line, copyright header, or
acknowledgement of any kind is a condition of this grant, and the copyright notice
above may be removed from any copy taken under it. Credit is welcome and never
expected: taking an idea, a method, or a whole file from here and shipping it as your
own is exactly what this section is for.

Scope and limits, stated plainly so nobody has to guess:

  - The grant is irrevocable as to any version of this code published under this
    licence. Withdrawing it later would make it worthless to rely on today, which
    would defeat the point of granting it.
  - It covers the code in this repository that its contributors own. It does not and
    cannot cover third-party code, which remains under its own licence -- see
    section 4.
  - It is a licence to the code, not a transfer of copyright, and not a trademark
    licence to the name "rstweaks".
  - The code is provided as-is under this grant, with no warranty of any kind and no
    liability on the part of its authors.

If you maintain a mod this project touches and you want something from here, take it.
If it is easier to ask than to read, ask -- but you do not have to.


3. PROVISIONAL, AND KNOWN TO BE

This is a provisional licence chosen to keep options open while the project is young.
It is not a considered long-term choice, and it has two known consequences worth
being aware of:

  1. Contributors retain copyright in their own contributions. This repository has
     already received work from someone other than the copyright holder above, so
     "All Rights Reserved" by a single party is a simplification -- and so is the
     grant in section 2, which for that contributor's work is only as good as their
     agreement to it. Contributions made after this licence was adopted are accepted
     on its terms, section 2 included. Before this project accepts contributions
     publicly, it wants either a real open-source licence or an explicit contributor
     agreement.

  2. All Rights Reserved discourages the things that usually help a mod: forks that
     fix it after it is abandoned, packs that need to patch it, and other developers
     reading it to learn from. Section 2 answers that only for upstream developers,
     which is the case this project actually cares about. Worth revisiting for
     everyone else before any public release.


4. OTHER PEOPLE'S CODE

This licence covers only the code in this repository. It does not apply to Refined
Storage, Cable Tiers, Step Crafter, Functional Storage, Sophisticated Core, or any
other mod this project depends on or interoperates with; those remain under their own
licences and are not redistributed here.
